    "events": [
      {
        "cell": [
          1,
          7
        ],
        "text": "A message is scratched into a half-submerged wall: \"THE SCHOOL FLOATS. FOLLOW THE BELLS.\" You don't know what that means yet.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          2,
          11
        ],
        "text": "Uncle Somchai's floating noodle-barge creaks against a submerged railing. His legs ended at the knee before the flood - what's below is salvaged hydro-turbine now. \"Buy, trade, or just stand there,\" he says, ladling something that used to be tom yum. \"Word is the transformer room north of here still has juice in it, if somebody's fool enough to wade in and hook it back up. Three breakers. Do 'em in order or you'll fry yourself for nothing - and I hear the current gate south of it won't open for anything less.\"",
        "repeatable": true
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          6,
          8
        ],
        "text": "Sister Da used to be a nurse. Now she runs awakenings out of a gutted pharmacy stall - no sedation, no guarantee you walk out the same rank you walked in. \"Half the Hunters down here found their class on my table,\" she says, wiping down a scalpel that's seen too much. \"The other half didn't wake up at all. Your call.\"",
        "repeatable": true
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          3,
          5
        ],
        "text": "Soi 11 Drowned Arcade - signs for a submerged entertainment center still hum under the water, arcade cabinets glowing green through six feet of scum. Something down there is still keeping score.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          21,
          2
        ],
        "text": "The BTS Asok platform rises just above the waterline through a locked gate to the east - the closest thing to solid, fortified ground left in the Shallows. Survivors camped here before most of them stopped camping anywhere. You'd need a keycard to get past the turnstile.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          8,
          2
        ],
        "text": "Cracked Cabinet - SKEE BALL: the screen still lights up when you wade past it. On a whim, you slap the coin return. It coughs up a token that shouldn't still work, and the machine chimes a tinny, ancient jingle.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "sets_flag": "arcade_1"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          14,
          4
        ],
        "text": "Cabinet: DANCE REVOLUTION - the token from Skee Ball fits the slot dead center. The arrows scroll, half-submerged, and you stomp through them anyway. High score achieved by absolutely nobody who's checking.",
        "fail_text": "This cabinet's coin slot is corroded shut - it wants the same kind of token the Skee Ball machine spat out, and you don't have one yet.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "arcade_1",
        "sets_flag": "arcade_2"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          19,
          1
        ],
        "text": "Ticket Booth: with two machines' worth of tickets jammed into the redemption slot, the booth's old prize case pops open with a wet crack. Inside, laminated and somehow still legible: a staff keycard for the BTS platform gate.",
        "fail_text": "The ticket booth's redemption slot stays dark - you haven't fed it enough machines yet.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "arcade_2",
        "sets_flag": "arcade_3",
        "reward_item": "bts_keycard"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          25,
          1
        ],
        "text": "The Asok survivor camp is long abandoned, but whoever left took only what they could carry - bedrolls, ration tins, a hand-crank radio still folded open to a dead station. Whoever they were, they left in a hurry, not a fight.",
        "repeatable": true
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          9,
          10
        ],
        "text": "Feeder Alpha: a battery cell wedged into a corroded relay atop a sunken taxi roof. You force the contacts together - the relay catches with a jolt, and the water around your boots crackles.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "sets_flag": "pump_alpha"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          12,
          9
        ],
        "text": "Feeder Beta: the second relay, one taxi roof over. With Alpha already live, the contacts bite clean on the first try. Two down.",
        "fail_text": "Feeder Beta's contacts are dead cold - nothing feeding it yet. Whatever's upstream of this one needs to go first.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "pump_alpha",
        "sets_flag": "pump_beta"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          14,
          11
        ],
        "text": "Feeder Gamma: the last relay, right at the transformer room's mouth. All three catch at once - the submerged room groans and drains, and somewhere south you hear the deep-water floodgate grind open.",
        "fail_text": "Feeder Gamma won't take a charge - the line's dead until Beta's carrying current.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "pump_beta",
        "sets_flag": "gate_drained",
        "reward_item": "salvaged_battery_cell"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          2,
          15
        ],
        "text": "A half-sunk stairwell drops even further down, into water that's gone perfectly still. Something about the stillness feels less like calm and more like waiting.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          24,
          15
        ],
        "text": "A waterproofed radio, still looping on a dead frequency. Under the static: an emergency broadcast, timestamped weeks before the flood hit. Canal lock closures \"for scheduled maintenance\" - the same locks that kept this whole district from draining. They knew. They picked who'd drown first.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "reward_item": "emergency_broadcast_chip"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          11,
          19
        ],
        "text": "The water is well over your head here if you stop moving - only momentum and shallow footing on submerged wreckage keep you above it. Whatever the Neon Strangler and the Mother in the deep water feed on, it isn't oxygen.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          0,
          18
        ],
        "text": "Someone built a shrine down here before the flood - joss sticks long dissolved, a brass bowl gone green. Someone else looted it, almost completely. They missed one thing, wedged behind the altar.",
        "repeatable": false
      }
    ]
  },
