    "events": [
      {
        "cell": [
          3,
          5
        ],
        "text": "Section 7 - the Amulet Vault. Heat-pulsing clay talismans are still stacked on their shelves in neat rows, like whoever priced them expects to come back.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          2,
          11
        ],
        "text": "Kru Viroj hunches over a folding table of waterlogged watches, obsessively winding ones that will never tick again. \"I can hear the flood's pulse,\" he says, not looking up. \"It has a rhythm, like a heartbeat that forgot how to stop. Section 7's vault only opens for a balanced scale - a real amulet against a cursed weight. Get either wrong and it stays shut forever. And whatever's past the vault, I wouldn't go looking for it.\"",
        "repeatable": true
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          6,
          8
        ],
        "text": "Someone's nailed a mannequin head to a stall post, facing north. Every stall past this point has one, all facing the same direction - toward whatever's being worshipped up there.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          21,
          2
        ],
        "text": "Through a gap in the collapsed stalls you can see the Vivarium gate to the east, chained shut from this side. Something in there is still moving, patient about it.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          8,
          2
        ],
        "text": "First Offering: a torn mannequin dress, folded neatly at the shrine's base among a dozen identical others. You add yours to the pile. Nothing happens. Yet.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "sets_flag": "mannequin_1"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          14,
          4
        ],
        "text": "Second Offering: a cracked porcelain face, set into a nook clearly shaped for exactly this. It clicks into place, and for a moment every mannequin head in sight turns half an inch.",
        "fail_text": "The nook stays empty without a first offering already given - the shrine reads them in order.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "mannequin_1",
        "sets_flag": "mannequin_2"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          19,
          1
        ],
        "text": "Third Offering: a curio bell, the last of the three. It rings once, and a hidden panel behind the shrine grinds open on a small brass key - just enough to bolt-cut a cage lock somewhere.",
        "fail_text": "The bell doesn't ring yet - the shrine wants a second offering first.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "mannequin_2",
        "sets_flag": "mannequin_3",
        "reward_item": "vivarium_cage_key"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          25,
          1
        ],
        "text": "The Vivarium Drains - ruptured exotic-wildlife holding cells, bars bent outward, not in. Whatever was in here didn't escape. It got out.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          26,
          3
        ],
        "text": "A waterlogged shipping crate, forced open. Trade manifests inside list \"biological samples\" arriving from a trench off the coast - dated days before the first fissure broke the riverbed. Somebody was expecting this.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "reward_item": "trade_manifest"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          9,
          10
        ],
        "text": "A corpse slumped against a collapsed stall, pockets still full. You pull a cursed lead weight from where a heart used to be. It's heavier than it should be.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "sets_flag": "has_lead_weight"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          12,
          9
        ],
        "text": "A brass scale bolted to Section 7's shelving. You set the lead weight on one side and a shelf amulet on the other. The arm tips, settles, and holds - this one's genuine.",
        "fail_text": "The scale's empty on one side. You'll need something with real weight to test an amulet against.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "has_lead_weight",
        "sets_flag": "amulet_balanced"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          14,
          11
        ],
        "text": "The vault door reads the balanced scale through a slot in the frame and grinds open, stacks of clay talismans humming in unison - and past them, a passage down that wasn't on any market map.",
        "fail_text": "The vault door won't budge - it's still waiting on a balanced scale, not just a weight.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "amulet_balanced",
        "sets_flag": "vault_opened",
        "reward_item": "genuine_amulet"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          2,
          15
        ],
        "text": "A stall padlock swings loose on a chain, cut clean through - somebody already tried force here and gave up. Whatever's past it probably still wants a real key.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          11,
          19
        ],
        "text": "The mud runs deeper the further south you wade, thick with the smell of animal musk that shouldn't still be this strong years later.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          0,
          18
        ],
        "text": "A shrine down here too, older and cruder than the one up north - just a mannequin head on a stake, ringed with dead stall lights. Someone's first attempt, maybe.",
        "repeatable": false
      }
    ]
  },
