    "events": [
      {
        "cell": [
          3,
          5
        ],
        "text": "Stack-City Core - a ten-story tower of rusted shipping containers, stacked and welded into something between a fortress and a grave. Rope ladders still sway between the upper tiers.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          1,
          9
        ],
        "text": "Commander Lek stands watch with one working eye and a rifle held like it's still useful. His F-rank scavengers work the mud around him, unbothered - or too scared to be. \"Crane's still standing over at the sluice gate,\" he says, not looking at you. \"Align the container bridges to it and you can cross without swimming. Do it in order - alpha bridge, beta bridge, then the crane lock - or the whole rig drops you in the sludge. Climb Stack-City's ladders if you want a dry place to sleep first - top tier's got a locked drydock, if you can get the tower to let you in.\"",
        "repeatable": true
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          6,
          8
        ],
        "text": "Rope ladders sway overhead between the container tiers, tied off by hands that stopped climbing a long time ago. Something up there still tends them.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          21,
          2
        ],
        "text": "From the top tier you can see Drydock 4 to the east, an oil tanker wedged sideways in the mud - and a gate that clearly wants more than just showing up.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          11,
          9
        ],
        "text": "A waterlogged strongbox, Lek's own handwriting on the ledgers inside. Shipping manifests routed through Ratchaprasong - food, going out, children coming back. The entries don't say what for. They don't have to.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "reward_item": "leks_militia_logs"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          8,
          2
        ],
        "text": "Ladder Tier 1: you lash the lowest rope ladder off to a stable container corner. It holds your weight without groaning. One tier secured.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "sets_flag": "ladder_1"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          14,
          4
        ],
        "text": "Ladder Tier 2: with the lower tier secure, this one's a clean climb - the ropes are old but the knots are sound. Two tiers up.",
        "fail_text": "This ladder's still coiled and unlashed - the tier below it needs securing first.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "ladder_1",
        "sets_flag": "ladder_2"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          19,
          1
        ],
        "text": "Ladder Tier 3: the top tier, and the view from here reaches past the sluice gate. A weatherproofed card is wedged into the railing - someone's old tower pass, still good.",
        "fail_text": "The top ladder's out of reach without the tier below it secured first.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "requires_flag": "ladder_2",
        "sets_flag": "ladder_3",
        "reward_item": "tower_access_card"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          25,
          1
        ],
        "text": "Drydock 4. An oil tanker, wedged sideways in the mud, hull split open like it was trying to give birth to something. Whatever it was already left.",
        "repeatable": false
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          4,
          5
        ],
        "text": "Bridge Alpha: you wedge a container flush against the crane's arm. It groans, but holds. One aligned.",
        "repeatable": false,
        "sets_flag": "bridge_alpha"
      },
      {
        "cell": [
          12,
          8
